result_text:
The diff is a pure rename: `redis_config` becomes `server_config` in both the global `config` struct and `clusterNode`, and all 14 uses in `src/valkey-benchmark.c` are updated. No uses of the old name are left in `src/`, `tests/` or `utils/`, so the rename is complete and doesn't change behaviour. No `.codegraph/` directory exists, and no CLAUDE.md rule covers C code here, so the conventions angle found nothing.

All six findings below are existing bugs inside functions this diff touches (`main`, `showLatencyReport`, `freeClusterNode`), not bugs the rename introduced. None were separately verified, as this review level specifies.

```json
[
  {
    "file": "src/valkey-benchmark.c",
    "line": 1950,
    "summary": "The command-parsing loop runs to i <= argc and checks `sds_args[i][0]` whenever i == start, before checking i == argc. That reads past the end of the argc-sized sds_args array.",
    "failure_scenario": "`valkey-benchmark SET a b \\;` (a trailing ';' separator): at i=3 the ';' sets start=4, then at i=4 (== argc == start) the code dereferences sds_args[4], an out-of-bounds heap read and a possible crash. The same happens when argc is 0 after --stdin realloc edge cases, since getSdsArrayFromArgv allocates exactly argc slots."
  },
  {
    "file": "src/valkey-benchmark.c",
    "line": 1998,
    "summary": "The custom-command exit path frees only config.server_config. In cluster mode the per-node `server_config` objects (and the cluster nodes) are never freed, because freeClusterNodes() is not called on either exit path of main.",
    "failure_scenario": "`valkey-benchmark --cluster SET k v`: each node's serverConfig from getServerConfig (line 1872) leaks at exit, and ASan/valgrind runs report leaked sds save/appendonly strings per node."
  },
  {
    "file": "src/valkey-benchmark.c",
    "line": 2205,
    "summary": "The default-suite exit path has the same problem: it frees config.server_config but never the cluster nodes' server_config.",
    "failure_scenario": "`valkey-benchmark --cluster -t set`: the node serverConfig objects and node structs leak at exit, and the renamed field is not covered by any cleanup."
  },
  {
    "file": "src/valkey-benchmark.c",
    "line": 1998,
    "summary": "The early `return 0` for custom commands skips `freeCliConnInfo(config.conn_info)` and `zfree(data)`-style cleanup that the default-suite path does at line 2204, so the two exit paths are inconsistent.",
    "failure_scenario": "`valkey-benchmark -a pass SET k v` under a leak checker: conn_info hostip/auth/user strings are reported as leaked, while the default suite path frees them."
  },
  {
    "file": "src/valkey-benchmark.c",
    "line": 899,
    "summary": "Non-cluster mode prints `config.server_config->save` directly, but cluster mode maps an empty save to \"NONE\" (line 894). Standalone output shows an empty value when persistence is disabled.",
    "failure_scenario": "Server with `save \"\"`: the standalone report prints `host configuration \"save\": ` (blank), while the cluster report prints `save: NONE` for the same config. Output is inconsistent and misleading."
  },
  {
    "file": "src/valkey-benchmark.c",
    "line": 1079,
    "summary": "freeClusterNode frees slots and server_config but not `node->updated_slots`, which updateClusterSlotsConfiguration allocates (line 1276).",
    "failure_scenario": "A slot update fills node->updated_slots, then fetchClusterConfiguration fails or re-runs and calls freeClusterNodes (line 1185) before the swap at line 1299. The CLUSTER_SLOTS*sizeof(int) buffer leaks."
  }
]
```
